    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>Système de cote ÉnerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="6" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.6b18345</English>
                <French>v15.6b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="16" build="18345">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.16b18345</English>
                <French>v1.16b18345</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



HRV Air duct vent in side wall is not sealed properly.



Dryer vent through back wall is not sealed properly.



Right side basement bedroom window is leaky.



Kitchen window frame is not sealed properly. 



Back Door is very leaky and should be replaced.



Attic hatch is quite leaky. Install a gasket around the base of the hatch and add rigid insulation to the top of the hatch to give it weight so it will compress the gasket and create a seal.



Right Master Bedroom sliding window is leaky. 



Existing Chimey should be removed and sealed properly.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>By adding 4" of type 2 EPS insulation to the exterior of the home, you would save up to 14 GJ of energy annually. The ERS Program only shows this as an addition of R-15, but there are materials available that would give you the nominal insulation value of R-20 for 4" of type 2 EPS.



The Energy Solutions Centre has an insulation upgrade available of $2.50/square foot of surface area when R-20 nominal insulation value is added to a building component. This surface area calculation would be wall area less windows and doors.



</mainWalls>
                <foundation>For above grade walls, see wall upgrade comments.</foundation>
                <windows>Upgrade 5 windows to ENERGY STAR® Zone 3 rated windows. 



Picture window upstairs

Window by front door

Right master bedroom sliding window

Basement living room window

Basement bedroom window



This upgrade will save 6 GJ of energy per year. 



 ENERGY STAR® Zone 3 windows are eligible for a $100 rebate per window to a maximum rebate of $1,000 per home.



Please contact Energy Solutions Centre for more details



http://goodenergyyukon.ca/renovations



</windows>
                <doors>Upgrade Solid wood back door to new steel ploystyrene filled door. This will decrease the amount of air leakage in the home and increase the thermal performance of the door. This will result is 1 Gigijoule (GJ) of energy savings annually.



Unfortunately the rebate is only for upgrading windows at the moment.



Check after the new fiscal year for new rebate programs from the Energy Solutions Centre.</doors>
                <HeatingSystem>Install programmable or smart thermostats for electric baseboards.</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
